IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-part8-ch1-no-requirements`

-- Part 8 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Chapter 2, regulations 112 to 114: moving sanctions from ESA or JSA,
-- failures for which no reduction is made, and the work placement that section 26(2)(a) of the Act prescribes.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).

§ `Chapter 2 — Miscellaneous`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 112 — Application of ESA or JSA sanctions to universal credit`

-- Schedule 11 has effect in relation to persons who are, or have been, entitled to an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's
-- allowance and who are, or become, entitled to universal credit. This is the scope of the rules in uc4-sch11-sanctions.l4.
-- src:1751 | Miscellaneous
-- src:1752 | 112 Application of ESA or JSA sanctions to universal credit
-- src:1753 | Schedule 11 has effect in relation to persons who are, or have been, entitled to an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance and who are, or become, entitled to universal credit.
@ref reg 112 (src:1751-1753)
GIVEN `the person is, or has been, entitled to an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is, or becomes, entitled to universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 112 — Schedule 11 has effect in relation to the person` `the person is, or has been, entitled to an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance` `the person is, or becomes, entitled to universal credit` MEANS
    `the person is, or has been, entitled to an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance`
    AND `the person is, or becomes, entitled to universal credit`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 113 — Failures for which no reduction is applied`

-- Paragraph (1): no reduction is made under section 26 or 27 of the Act for a sanctionable failure in any of seven cases (a) to (g). Each is
-- a rule below, and the rule for the paragraph is the "or" of the seven. Regulation 113 does not say what a sanctionable failure is; that
-- is sections 26 and 27 of the Act.
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
-- src:1754 | 113 Failures for which no reduction is applied
-- src:1755 | (1) No reduction is to be made under section 26 or 27 of the Act for a sanctionable failure where—
-- src:1756 | (a) the sanctionable failure is listed in section 26(2)(b) or (c) (failure to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work, or failure to take up an offer of paid work) and the vacancy is because of a strike arising from a trade dispute;
-- src:1757 | (b) the sanctionable failure is listed in section 26(2)(d) (claimant ceases paid work or loses pay), and the following circumstances apply—
-- src:1758 | (i) the claimant's work search and work availability requirements are subject to limitations imposed under section 17(4) and 18(3) in respect of work available for a certain number of hours,
-- src:1759 | (ii) the claimant takes up paid work, or is in paid work and takes up more paid work that is for a greater number of hours, and
-- src:1760 | (iii) the claimant voluntarily ceases that paid work, or more paid work, or loses pay, within a trial period;
-- src:1761 | (c) the sanctionable failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work, or loses pay, because of a strike arising from a trade dispute;
-- src:1762 | (d) the sanctionable failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work as a member of the regular or reserve forces, or loses pay in that capacity;
-- src:1763 | (e) the sanctionable failure is listed in section 26(4) (failure to take up an offer of paid work, or to cease paid work or lose pay before making a claim), and the period of the reduction that would otherwise apply under regulation 102(4) is the same as, or shorter than, the number of days beginning with the day after the date of the sanctionable failure and ending with the date of claim;
-- src:1764 | (f) the sanctionable failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work in one of the following circumstances—
-- src:1765 | (i) the claimant has been dismissed because of redundancy after volunteering or agreeing to be dismissed,
-- src:1766 | (ii) the claimant has ceased work on an agreed date without being dismissed in pursuance of an agreement relating to voluntary redundancy, or
-- src:1767 | (iii) the claimant has been laid-off or kept on short-time to the extent specified in section 148 of the Employment Rights Act 1996, and has complied with the requirements of that section; or
-- src:1768 | (g) the sanctionable failure is that the claimant by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, ceases paid work or loses pay, but the claimant's monthly earnings (or, if the claimant is a member of a couple, their joint monthly earnings) have not fallen below the amount specified in regulation 99(6) (circumstances in which requirements must not be imposed).
-- src:1769 | (2) In this regulation “regular or reserve forces” has the same meaning as in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006 .
-- Limb (a): the failure is listed in section 26(2)(b) or (c) (failure to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work, or failure to take up an
-- offer of paid work) and the vacancy is because of a strike arising from a trade dispute.
@ref reg 113(1)(a) (src:1756)
GIVEN `the failure is listed in section 26(2)(b) or (c) of the Act (failure to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work, or failure to take up an offer of paid work)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy is because of a strike arising from a trade dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 113(1)(a) — no reduction: a vacancy because of a strike` `the failure is listed in section 26(2)(b) or (c) of the Act (failure to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work, or failure to take up an offer of paid work)` `the vacancy is because of a strike arising from a trade dispute` MEANS
    `the failure is listed in section 26(2)(b) or (c) of the Act (failure to apply for a particular vacancy for paid work, or failure to take up an offer of paid work)`
    AND `the vacancy is because of a strike arising from a trade dispute`

-- Limb (b): the failure is listed in section 26(2)(d) (claimant ceases paid work or loses pay), and (i) the claimant's work search and work
-- availability requirements are subject to limitations under sections 17(4) and 18(3) in respect of work available for a certain number of
-- hours, (ii) the claimant takes up paid work, or is in paid work and takes up more paid work that is for a greater number of hours, and
-- (iii) the claimant voluntarily ceases that paid work, or more paid work, or loses pay, within a trial period.
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
-- out of range: sections 15 to 18 and 23 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which requirement is in question, and its limits, are stated inputs
@ref reg 113(1)(b) (src:1757-1760)
GIVEN `the failure is listed in section 26(2)(d) of the Act (claimant ceases paid work or loses pay)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's work search and work availability requirements are subject to limitations imposed under section 17(4) and 18(3) in respect of work available for a certain number of hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant takes up paid work, or is in paid work and takes up more paid work that is for a greater number of hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant voluntarily ceases that paid work, or more paid work, or loses pay, within a trial period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 113(1)(b) — no reduction: ceasing paid work or losing pay within a trial period` `the failure is listed in section 26(2)(d) of the Act (claimant ceases paid work or loses pay)` `the claimant's work search and work availability requirements are subject to limitations imposed under section 17(4) and 18(3) in respect of work available for a certain number of hours` `the claimant takes up paid work, or is in paid work and takes up more paid work that is for a greater number of hours` `the claimant voluntarily ceases that paid work, or more paid work, or loses pay, within a trial period` MEANS
    `the failure is listed in section 26(2)(d) of the Act (claimant ceases paid work or loses pay)`
    AND `the claimant's work search and work availability requirements are subject to limitations imposed under section 17(4) and 18(3) in respect of work available for a certain number of hours`
    AND `the claimant takes up paid work, or is in paid work and takes up more paid work that is for a greater number of hours`
    AND `the claimant voluntarily ceases that paid work, or more paid work, or loses pay, within a trial period`

-- Limb (c): the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work, or loses pay, because of a strike arising from a trade dispute.
@ref reg 113(1)(c) (src:1761)
GIVEN `the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work, or loses pay, because of a strike arising from a trade dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 113(1)(c) — no reduction: ceasing paid work or losing pay because of a strike` `the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work, or loses pay, because of a strike arising from a trade dispute` MEANS
    `the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work, or loses pay, because of a strike arising from a trade dispute`

-- Limb (d): the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work as a member of the regular or reserve forces, or loses pay in that
-- capacity. "Regular or reserve forces" has the meaning in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006 (paragraph (2)).
@ref reg 113(1)(d) (src:1762)
GIVEN `the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work as a member of the regular or reserve forces, or loses pay in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 113(1)(d) — no reduction: ceasing paid work in the regular or reserve forces` `the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work as a member of the regular or reserve forces, or loses pay in that capacity` MEANS
    `the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work as a member of the regular or reserve forces, or loses pay in that capacity`

-- Limb (e): the failure is listed in section 26(4) (failure to take up an offer of paid work, or to cease paid work or lose pay before making a
-- claim) and the period of the reduction that would otherwise apply under regulation 102(4) is the same as, or shorter than, the number of
-- days beginning with the day after the date of the failure and ending with the date of claim. If regulation 102(4) gives no period (NOTHING),
-- the comparison cannot be made and the limb is not met.
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
@ref reg 113(1)(e) (src:1763)
GIVEN `the failure is listed in section 26(4) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of the reduction that would otherwise apply under regulation 102(4)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `date of the sanctionable failure` IS A DATE
      `date of claim` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 113(1)(e) — no reduction: a pre-claim failure whose reduction is used up by the days before the claim` `the failure is listed in section 26(4) of the Act` `the period of the reduction that would otherwise apply under regulation 102(4)` `date of the sanctionable failure` `date of claim` MEANS
    `the failure is listed in section 26(4) of the Act`
    AND `the reduction is no longer than the days before the claim`
    WHERE
        `the reduction is no longer than the days before the claim` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the period of the reduction that would otherwise apply under regulation 102(4)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST period THEN period AT MOST (Day `date of claim` MINUS Day `date of the sanctionable failure`)

-- Limb (f): the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work in one of the following circumstances: (i) dismissed because of
-- redundancy after volunteering or agreeing to be dismissed; (ii) ceased work on an agreed date without being dismissed in pursuance of an
-- agreement relating to voluntary redundancy; (iii) laid off or kept on short-time to the extent specified in section 148 of the Employment
-- Rights Act 1996, and has complied with the requirements of that section.
-- out of range: sections 86 and 148 of the Employment Rights Act 1996 (not among the inputs): the facts they describe are stated inputs
@ref reg 113(1)(f) (src:1764-1767)
GIVEN `the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has been dismissed because of redundancy after volunteering or agreeing to be dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has ceased work on an agreed date without being dismissed in pursuance of an agreement relating to voluntary redundancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has been laid-off or kept on short-time to the extent specified in section 148 of the Employment Rights Act 1996, and has complied with the requirements of that section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 113(1)(f) — no reduction: ceasing paid work in a redundancy or lay-off` `the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work` `the claimant has been dismissed because of redundancy after volunteering or agreeing to be dismissed` `the claimant has ceased work on an agreed date without being dismissed in pursuance of an agreement relating to voluntary redundancy` `the claimant has been laid-off or kept on short-time to the extent specified in section 148 of the Employment Rights Act 1996, and has complied with the requirements of that section` MEANS
    `the failure is that the claimant voluntarily ceases paid work`
    AND `one of the three circumstances`
    WHERE
        `one of the three circumstances` MEANS
            `the claimant has been dismissed because of redundancy after volunteering or agreeing to be dismissed`
            OR `the claimant has ceased work on an agreed date without being dismissed in pursuance of an agreement relating to voluntary redundancy`
            OR `the claimant has been laid-off or kept on short-time to the extent specified in section 148 of the Employment Rights Act 1996, and has complied with the requirements of that section`

-- Limb (g): the failure is that the claimant, by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, ceases paid work or loses pay, but
-- the claimant's monthly earnings (or, if a member of a couple, their joint monthly earnings) have not fallen below the amount specified in
-- regulation 99(6). For a member of a couple the joint earnings are held to the amount for 29 hours of paragraph (6)(b), and otherwise the
-- claimant's earnings to the amount for 18 hours of paragraph (6)(a) (fork F-113-1). The earnings are those after the failure.
-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
@ref reg 113(1)(g) (src:1768)
GIVEN `the failure is that the claimant by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, ceases paid work or loses pay` IS A BOOLEAN
      basis IS A `Claim basis`
      `the monthly earnings of the claimant, or the joint monthly earnings if the claimant is a member of a couple, after the failure` IS A NUMBER
      `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 113(1)(g) — no reduction: earnings have not fallen below the amount in regulation 99(6)` `the failure is that the claimant by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, ceases paid work or loses pay` basis `the monthly earnings of the claimant, or the joint monthly earnings if the claimant is a member of a couple, after the failure` `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations` MEANS
    `the failure is that the claimant by reason of misconduct, or voluntarily and for no good reason, ceases paid work or loses pay`
    AND `the earnings have not fallen below the amount`
    WHERE
        `the earnings have not fallen below the amount` MEANS
            IF `reg 2 — the claimant has a partner` basis
            THEN `reg 99(6)(b) — the couple's combined monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 29 hours` basis `the monthly earnings of the claimant, or the joint monthly earnings if the claimant is a member of a couple, after the failure` `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`
            ELSE `reg 99(6)(a) — the claimant's monthly earnings equal or exceed the amount for 18 hours` `the monthly earnings of the claimant, or the joint monthly earnings if the claimant is a member of a couple, after the failure` `the hourly rate set out in regulation 4 of the National Minimum Wage Regulations`

-- Paragraph (1): no reduction for a failure in any of cases (a) to (g).
@ref reg 113(1) (src:1755)
GIVEN `case (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `case (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `case (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `case (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `case (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `case (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `case (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 113(1) — no reduction is made for the failure` `case (a)` `case (b)` `case (c)` `case (d)` `case (e)` `case (f)` `case (g)` MEANS
    `case (a)` OR `case (b)` OR `case (c)` OR `case (d)` OR `case (e)` OR `case (f)` OR `case (g)`

-- Paragraph (2): "regular or reserve forces" has the same meaning as in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006 (coverage row: inert, a pure
-- citation; limb (d) takes the fact as a stated input).
-- src:1769 | (2) In this regulation “regular or reserve forces” has the same meaning as in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006 .
@ref reg 113(2) (src:1769)
`reg 113(2) — "regular or reserve forces" has the meaning in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006` MEANS
        "In this regulation regular or reserve forces has the same meaning as in section 374 of the Armed Forces Act 2006."

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 114 — Sanctionable failures under section 26 - work placements`

-- Paragraph (2): "the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme" means a scheme provided under arrangements made by the Secretary of State and known by that
-- name, designed to provide work or work-related activity for up to 30 hours per week over a period of 4 consecutive weeks with a view to
-- assisting claimants to improve their prospects of obtaining employment. "A period of 4 consecutive weeks" is exactly 4 (fork F-114-1).
-- src:1770 | 114 Sanctionable failures under section 26 - work placements
-- src:1771 | (1) A placement on the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme is a prescribed placement for the purpose of section 26(2)(a) of the Act (sanctionable failure not to comply with a work placement).
-- src:1772 | (2) In paragraph (1) “the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme” means a scheme provided pursuant to arrangements made by the Secretary of State and known by that name that is designed to provide work or work-related activity for up to 30 hours per week over a period of 4 consecutive weeks with a view to assisting claimants to improve their prospects of obtaining employment.
@ref reg 114(2) (src:1770-1772)
GIVEN `the scheme is provided pursuant to arrangements made by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme is known by the name Mandatory Work Activity Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the most hours a week of work or work-related activity that the scheme is designed to provide` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of consecutive weeks over which the scheme is designed to provide it` IS A NUMBER
      `the scheme is designed with a view to assisting claimants to improve their prospects of obtaining employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 114(2) — the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme` `the scheme is provided pursuant to arrangements made by the Secretary of State` `the scheme is known by the name Mandatory Work Activity Scheme` `the most hours a week of work or work-related activity that the scheme is designed to provide` `the number of consecutive weeks over which the scheme is designed to provide it` `the scheme is designed with a view to assisting claimants to improve their prospects of obtaining employment` MEANS
    `the scheme is provided pursuant to arrangements made by the Secretary of State`
    AND `the scheme is known by the name Mandatory Work Activity Scheme`
    AND (`the most hours a week of work or work-related activity that the scheme is designed to provide` AT MOST 30)
    AND (`the number of consecutive weeks over which the scheme is designed to provide it` EQUALS 4)
    AND `the scheme is designed with a view to assisting claimants to improve their prospects of obtaining employment`

-- Paragraph (1): a placement on the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme is a prescribed placement for the purpose of section 26(2)(a) of the Act
-- (sanctionable failure not to comply with a work placement).
-- src:1771 | (1) A placement on the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme is a prescribed placement for the purpose of section 26(2)(a) of the Act (sanctionable failure not to comply with a work placement).
@ref reg 114(1) (src:1771)
GIVEN `the placement is on a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme is the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 114(1) — the placement is a prescribed placement for section 26(2)(a) of the Act` `the placement is on a scheme` `the scheme is the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme` MEANS
    `the placement is on a scheme` AND `the scheme is the Mandatory Work Activity Scheme`
